<title>BRAZIL: CVRD 1996 net rises to 517 mln reais.</title>
<headline>CVRD 1996 net rises to 517 mln reais.</headline>
<dateline>RIO DE JANEIRO 1997-03-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Soon-to-be-privatized state mining giant Companhia Vale do Rio Doce posted the following 1996 results.</p>
<p>			   1996			 1995</p>
<p>    Net profit	 517 million		 328 million</p>
<p>    Gross revenue  2.878 bln		   2.419 bln</p>
<p>    Net revenue    2.743 bln		   2.284 bln</p>
<p>Note: All figures in Brazilian reais and in accordance with Brazilian Generally Accepted Accounting Principles.</p>
<p>The profit increase is due to a rise in international iron ore prices, cost-reduction measures and tax exemptions on exports.</p>
<p>((--Simona de Logu, Rio de Janeiro Newsroom, 5521 507 4151))</p>
</text>
